data: {"node_id": "reasoner_node", "label": "Reasoner", "type": "reasoner", "status": "completed", "description": "Analyzing data and deciding next action...", "output": {"messages": [{"content": "", "additional_kwargs": {"reasoning_content": "We have the restaurant profile: current food cost 55% vs target 30%. The user says Smash Burger cost inflated, app says cost 45 to make a single burger. The data shows recorded cost 4535 cents = €45.35. Computed cost 4660 cents = €46.60. So indeed cost high.\n\nWe need to investigate root causes. The audit shows line items:\n\n- Blend Smash Burger (wagyu mix): quantity 150 grams, catalog purchase unit kilograms, conversion rate 1000. Computed cost 375 cents = €3.75. That seems plausible.\n\n- Pan Brioche: 1 unit, cost 35 cents = €0.35. plausible.\n\n- Aceite de Trufa Negra: quantity 500 milliliters, catalog purchase unit liters, conversion rate 1000. Computed cost 4250 cents = €42.50. That is huge. 500 ml of truffle oil at €42.50 cost. That seems wrong. Likely unit mismatch: 500 ml but conversion rate 1000 means 1 liter = 1000 ml. But if purchase unit is liters, conversion rate 1000 means 1 liter = 1000 units? Wait: conversion_rate is likely purchase_unit to recipe_unit. If purchase unit is liters, recipe unit milliliters, conversion_rate 1000 means 1 liter = 1000 ml. That is correct. But cost 4250 cents for 500 ml means price per liter is 8500 cents = €85. That is high but maybe truffle oil is expensive. But 500 ml is huge for a burger. Usually 5-10 ml. So quantity anomaly: 500 ml is unrealistic. So likely user entered 500 ml instead of 5 ml. That explains inflated cost.\n\nAlso computed cost 4660 cents vs recorded 4535 cents difference 125 cents. But main issue is truffle oil quantity.\n\nAlso overall food cost 55% high. Could be due to miscategorised ingredients. Let's check ingredient catalog for food category.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "fc_5f4f1588-3d47-473d-812e-22e89dddb01c", "function": {"arguments": "{\"category\":\"food\",\"restaurant_id\":\"rest_310\"}", "name": "get_ingredient_catalog"}, "type": "function"}]}, "response_metadata": {"token_usage": {"completion_tokens": 454, "prompt_tokens": 1715, "total_tokens": 2169, "completion_time": 0.470598056, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 427}, "prompt_time": 0.045759276, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 1024}, "queue_time": 0.015691894, "total_time": 0.516357332}, "model_name": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_4970ff9dda", "service_tier": "on_demand", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "logprobs": null, "model_provider": "groq"}, "type": "ai", "name": null, "id": "lc_run--019d9097-b48b-7ce1-a8bb-b758ab579c00-0", "tool_calls": [{"name": "get_ingredient_catalog", "args": {"category": "food", "restaurant_id": "rest_310"}}], "invalid_tool_calls": [], "usage_metadata": {"input_tokens": 1715, "output_tokens": 454, "total_tokens": 2169, "input_token_details": {"cache_read": 1024}, "output_token_details": {"reasoning": 427}}}], "react_iterations": 4}, "step": 8}

